        <p>• IT is recorded as a musical fact, that every ' orchestra contains two " musicia.ners " wita, moustaches, one with spectacles, two with bald !heads, and, lastly, a very modest man with a ; white cravat, and that he from the force of cir- , curnstanees, always plays upon a brass instru- ment. "Wiry don't you trade with me?" said a close-fisted warehouseman to an acquaintance the other day. "Because," was the characteristic , reply, "You have never asked me, sir. I have looked all through the newspaper for an invitation, :in the shape of an advertisement, but in vain. I never go where I am not wanted.' A TRAMP who asked for breakfast at a farm- iimuse, and was refused a single crust, exclaimed with an injured air, "Alas, how deceptive is human 'stare! For two nights I have slept in your barn, -en of your apples, and drunk your cider, and now treat me as an utter stranger who has no claim "our friendship." -, where have you been?" "We have been 7, father." "We ! Who swam with you, "Nobody, sir." "Well, but you said swimming,' didn't you ? " "We have -kg, father." "Who did you swim • young rascal ? " "I ? I swam with The youn,4ster hardly dodged a ',sent at his head.</p>
