        <p>The Parliamentary Committee of the Trade Unions Congress are meeting this week in London to.pre- pare their programme for the next session. I under- stand that the Committee, in conjunction with th e London Trades Council, are contemplating holding a monster demonstratiou in Hyde Park to protest against the action taken by the house of Lords in reference to the Employers' biability Bill. The various trade unions in the United Kingdom will be asked to send representatives to this gathering, which will be held as soon as arrangements can be completed. It, is expeeted that the demonstration will exceed in point of numbers and importance that which took place some ten years ago when the Peers rejected the Franchise Bill.</p>
