        <head>'HOIST WITH HIS• OWN PETARD.*'</head>
        <p>'HOIST WITH HIS• OWN PETARD.*'</p>
        <p>A man, fearfully mutilated, was found near the Re 3 'at Observatory at Greenvvich,on Thursday night, and isle&amp; tr him the remnants of an exploded bomb. The injure, d parson was takon.to the hospital, where he died. Th a police, believe, it is said, that the man was a chief a a gang of foreign Anarchists.</p>
        <p>WIDNES TOWN COUNCIL, • , t I:fia</p>
        <p>--- The Quarterly meeting of this Akan&amp; NW, h1:.1 Lin the'Viiwn. flail on Tuesday afternoon i "Present Aldermen Sadler, Wareing, Williamson, Titamis, Tilley; Councill'ors`Owene, Hodgkinson, O'Donnell, Gough, Quinn, Singleton, DaVies, Smith, Shuttle- worth, G. I, Xeil, Christie, Barlow, Bullough, Wright, Longton; 11.53. Oppeulaeim (town clerk), S. floyle (accountant), 1. Carr (engineer), J. S. Sinclair (surveyor), W. Lowe (nuisance inspector), Dr. O'Keeffe (medical officer).</p>
        <p>•• • • Therown Clerk announced that the Mayor had left home for the benefit of 'his health, and he had appointed Alderman Sadler, deputy maypr, in his absence:—Alder- man Waring moved and Alderman Timin6seconded that Alderman Sadler be chairman, and the motion was carried unanimously. • 7.1315 ALDERILANIC ROBES. Councillor Barlow said it had been decided that like aldermen should appear in robes at the next meeting of the Council. Ile wished to know whether they had got the robes under their coats or where. (Laughter.)— Alderman Thurnis wished to know if it were recorded that, he voted against the motion. He was still of opinion that it was ridiculous and preposterous mum- mery and 'he declined to be bound by the resolution.— The illerk said the names nf those who voted were not recorded with respect to the robes, the Mayor's absense from the borough, he supposed, accounted for the alder- men appearin,, in their ordinary costume that day. (A laugh.)—Der. Barlow : I don't see that that is any reason.—llderman Williamson said if Alderman Timmis intended to vete against aldermen wearing robes he shot2ld havelcirmed his ainendment differently, and nsatde it read that aldermen do not wear robes instead of all the coUncillers as weans aldermen wear robes.</p>
