        <p>kj V U M . " CLEM ONT HOUSE, LITTLE SANGHOLL, NEAR CHESTER. 2nd Januar:7, 1694. MY. Jos. THORLEY, King's Cross, London. - It may be of interest to you to know the follow- ing On the 2nd October last, I purchased 13 Hens and a Cock—all cross-bred—and a very miserable lot they looked ; in fact, they had been half famished. I gave them hot food in the morning—boiled potatoes and meal, with dripping, bacon liquor, or such like stuff in it—and every other day about a teaspoonful of OVUM well mixed up. Result : up to prnent date, 2nd January, 513 eggs. Not a bad record, eh ? especially seeing that four were old Hens. OVUM is GRAND Stuff. Yours truly, WM. CORFIELD. "0 V U M Is sold in Cares containing 72 Packets, Cs., also in Bags-325., cwt. ; 15s. 6d., cwt. ; Si. 6d. lcwt. ;and Ss., 71b., carriage paid. JOSEPH THORLEY, KING'S pßoss, LONDON.</p>
